<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Flat, qualifier-free copies of each palette's canvas/ink/accent, for the "Light
  palette" / "Dark palette" pickers in Settings.

  Those two pickers must show a palette's true light colours AND its true dark colours
  at the same time, regardless of which mode is currently forced — something @color/
  names that vary by values-night cannot do, since only one value is resolvable per
  configuration. This is the same sanctioned direct-@color/ exception CLAUDE.md already
  carves out for the swatch dots themselves; these are just light/dark-locked copies of
  values already authored in lp_palette_<name>.xml and its values-night twin.

  Adding a ninth palette means one row here, alongside its lp_palette_*.xml pair.
-->
<resources>

